# The working copy ends its lines the way the repository does, with a line
# feed, on every machine. Without this, Git for Windows checks the files out
# with carriage returns, gofmt sees a file it did not write and lists the
# whole project, and golangci-lint says the same thing — while the committed
# content was right all along. The confusion costs an evening; this line
# costs nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf
